Batch the per-repo LFS checksum lookup in collect_hf_siblings.

GET /api/{repo_type}s/{namespace}/{name} resolves the HuggingFace
`siblings` list by calling collect_hf_siblings(), which resolved the
local LFS sha256 with one `get_file()` query per object. For a dataset
with ~40k files (~34k of them LFS-tracked) that is ~34k point lookups
per request; acl26-csr measured 16-17 s wall clock, scaling linearly
with file count (WMT_Project 443 files -> 0.19 s, openalex 5.2k ->
2.2 s). The sibling list only needs path -> sha256, so read the
repository's slice of the File table once and index it in memory.

Behaviour is unchanged: an empty stored sha256 still falls back to the
LakeFS-reported checksum, and non-LFS siblings are unaffected.

